{"base_rate":0.42181340341655715,"brier":0.14255059132720105,"bss":0.4155052322288304,"bss_hi":0.4919984267747872,"bss_lo":0.3350046641896552,"chart":{"base":[609.0,54.2],"fp":[248.7,295.6],"lead":"62,198.6 272,185.4 482,142.4 692,61.6","note":{"base":"skill 0.42 — higher than 77% of cities","fp":"low end +5pp, high end +17pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.6 °C — better than 12% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 6%; promised 96% → rained 80%"},"rel":"66.4,441.2 286.7,304 667.3,120.4"},"country":"AT","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09093298291721416,"ess":348.78729016219353,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Salzburg</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Salzburg rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>82%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>6%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSALZBURG, 3.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.42, ranked 49 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(24&ndash;83) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>296</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>84</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>72%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>82%</b></td><td class='num'>234</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Salzburg</b> <span class=\"muted\">Austria</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.42</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>24&ndash;83\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Salzburg &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Salzburg\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"60.475608108108105,375.85135135135135 125.13357142857143,282.3333333333333 249.6257894736842,147.31578947368422 359.5481690140845,43.63380281690144 409.8517948717948,18.0 409.8517948717948,24.22222222222223 359.5481690140845,105.15492957746477 249.6257894736842,228.73684210526318 125.13357142857143,343.0 60.475608108108105,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"228.45992115637318\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"228.45992115637318\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"60.475608108108105,361.0945945945946 125.13357142857143,295.33333333333337 249.6257894736842,190.42105263157896 359.5481690140845,120.53521126760563 409.8517948717948,81.77777777777777\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 296 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"60.475608108108105\" cy=\"361.0945945945946\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 19%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 84 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"125.13357142857143\" cy=\"295.33333333333337\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 54%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"249.6257894736842\" cy=\"190.42105263157896\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 72% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"359.5481690140845\" cy=\"120.53521126760563\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 82% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 234 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.8517948717948\" cy=\"81.77777777777777\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(42%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Salzburg the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.54) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.16).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.155</td><td class='num'>16.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.327</td><td class='num'>12.8%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>52%</td><td class='num'>0.530</td><td class='num'>6.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>217</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>0.539</td><td class='num'>8.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":47.79941,"lon":13.04399,"n":761,"n_cities":213,"name":"Salzburg","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.006993243243243244,"n":296,"obs":0.057432432432432436,"sig":true},{"hi":0.38,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.18964285714285714,"n":84,"obs":0.23809523809523808,"sig":false},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.38,"mean":0.5413157894736842,"n":76,"obs":0.5263157894736842,"sig":false},{"hi":0.95,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.851830985915493,"n":71,"obs":0.7183098591549296,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.95,"mean":0.9939316239316238,"n":234,"obs":0.8247863247863247,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.3,"provisional":false,"rank":49,"rank_hi":83.0,"rank_lo":24.0,"reliability":0.011731812755495216,"resolution":0.1145944135297644,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"salzburg","station":"SALZBURG","timezone":"Europe/Vienna"}